expected_issues.description:
Potential bug/footgun: `.set(person)` includes `id`. This may attempt to update the primary key (or at least send it in the SET clause), which is typically unintended and may error. Prefer destructuring to exclude `id` from the patch before calling `.set()`.

```suggestion
  async update(person: Updateable<Person> & { id: string }) {
    const { id, ...patch } = person;
    return this.db
      .updateTable('person')
      .set(patch)
      .where('person.id', '=', id)
      .returningAll()
      .executeTakeFirstOrThrow();
  }
```

