known_false_positives.description:
`movePersonFile` requires `thumbnailPath: string`, but the method early-exits only when `oldPath` is falsy inside `moveFile`. If `thumbnailPath` can legitimately be empty for some persons (newly created, incomplete data), consider adding an explicit guard here and logging/throwing a clear error so the caller can react, rather than silently doing nothing.

Same as above: consider `Pick<PersonEntity, 'id' | 'ownerId' | 'thumbnailPath'>` or a shared type to avoid repeating inline object types.

```suggestion
  async movePersonFile(
    person: Pick<PersonEntity, 'id' | 'ownerId' | 'thumbnailPath'>,
    pathType: PersonPathType,
  ) {
    const { id: entityId, thumbnailPath } = person;
    if (!thumbnailPath) {
      this.logger.warn(`Missing thumbnailPath for person ${entityId}`);
      return;
    }
